id: SEC-027
title: Buffer over-read with user-controlled length (CVE-2014-0160 Heartbleed)
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .c .cpp .cc .h .hpp
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ .git/ build/
patterns:
  - regex: memcpy\(.*,.*,.*\blen(gth)?\b
    message: "memcpy with variable length — ensure bounds checking before copy (Heartbleed pattern: CVE-2014-0160)"
  - regex: memcpy\(.*,.*,.*\bsize\b
    message: "memcpy with variable size — validate size against buffer capacity before copy"
  - regex: memcpy\(.*,.*,.*\bn\b\)
    message: "memcpy with parameter n — ensure n does not exceed source/destination buffer size"
fix: Always validate that the length parameter does not exceed the buffer size before memcpy/memmove calls.